#   npx skills add mager/frontend-design
# (~2.8M of CSV design data + scripts, installed by
# (2026-09-14). IGNORED: everything else under .claude/ — the vendored UI/UX Pro Max skill set
# `npm i -g ui-ux-pro-max-cli && uipro init --ai claude`), reinstallable in one command and
# a second source of truth for RBAC and config, which is exactly how the hand-written
# adversarial review pass, the session change log, the end-to-end walk, the mermaid-ascii terminal
# Agent skills installed with `npx skills add`. Third-party content, per-developer tooling,
# and not part of what this repository ships — the same reasoning that keeps .env and the
# below and is recreated by the `npx skills add` there; and settings.local.json, personal by
# change-log hook and the read-only permission rules; the operator's process lives in them
# Cluster CA bundles: environment-specific and regenerable from kubeconfig
# definition.
# deploy/dashboard.yaml went 62 commits stale while still looking authoritative.
# it embeds the oauth cookie secret read from the live cluster, and a checked-in copy becomes
# it is the chart rendered for inspection and testing. Two reasons it must not be committed —
# make the tree dirty: the build scripts derive an image tag from the commit and refuse to
# preview — and the project settings that carry the
# Registry credentials — never commit. .env.example carries the placeholders instead.
# Rendered chart output (local-development/render-manifests.sh). Generated, never authored:
# rendered deploy/ folder out. Reinstall with:
# Session hand-off notes and design scratch — deliberately untracked, but they must not
# stamp one that no commit reproduces.
# The project's Claude Code directory. TRACKED: the four hand-written project skills — the
# tooling, not product; the frontend-design symlink, which points into the ignored .agents/ tree
